    <briefdescription>
<para>Wrapper to abstract locks during verification. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Abstracts a lock implementation such that in compilations for verification, ie, with VSYNC_VERIFICATION defined, the lock will be replaced by a pthread_mutex, which greatly helps the model checkers. On normal compilation the given concrete lock will be used.</para>
<para><linebreak/>
<linebreak/>
### Example:<linebreak/>
<linebreak/>
</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".c"><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;<ref refid="ticketlock_8h" kindref="compound" tooltip="Classic ticketlock with two 32-bit variables (owner and next).">vsync/spinlock/ticketlock.h</ref>&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&lt;<ref refid="abstract__lock_8h" kindref="compound" tooltip="Wrapper to abstract locks during verification.">vsync/utils/abstract_lock.h</ref>&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="abstract__lock_8h_1a0a578d0ff996fcd10b338fe93f5e9c2f" kindref="member" tooltip="Defines an abstract lock type and functions to initialize, acquire, and release it.">DEF_ABSTRACT_LOCK</ref><sp/>(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>my_lock,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>the<sp/>prefix<sp/>for<sp/>type<sp/>and<sp/>functions</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="structticketlock__s" kindref="compound">ticketlock_t</ref>,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>the<sp/>type<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>base<sp/>lock</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="ticketlock_8h_1ac3d4fe569733d86bcbf7718076315f73" kindref="member" tooltip="Initializes the ticketlock.">ticketlock_init</ref>,<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>init,<sp/>acquire<sp/>and<sp/>release<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>base<sp/>lock</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="ticketlock_8h_1a0dd64bcd770b5a1dc3bcf77e62b33733" kindref="member" tooltip="Acquires the ticketlock.">ticketlock_acquire</ref>,</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="ticketlock_8h_1a32c25963b2b0cf25ce3dfb407aa8f844" kindref="member" tooltip="Releases the ticketlock.">ticketlock_release</ref>,</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="ticketlock_8h_1aaa94462de9f9e38124f88e07da1ecea2" kindref="member" tooltip="Tries to acquire the ticketlock.">ticketlock_tryacquire</ref></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>This defines <computeroutput>struct my_lock_s</computeroutput> as well as a type <computeroutput>my_lock_t</computeroutput>. It also defines <computeroutput>_init</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>_acquire</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>_release</computeroutput> functions with the <computeroutput>my_lock</computeroutput> prefix. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
